# Manifest for avformat.rs / swscale.rs transcription (libavformat 63, libswscale 10)
#
# Note: AVIndexEntry (libavformat/avformat.h) contains C bitfields
# (`int flags:2; int size:30;`) after `timestamp`. Only its leading `pos`
# and `timestamp` are transcribed (as a PREFIX, read through pointers
# returned by avformat_index_get_entry_from_timestamp), so no bitfield had
# to be represented in Rust. No bitfields were encountered in any
# transcribed struct.
#
# FF_API_* gate evaluation (LIBAVFORMAT_VERSION_MAJOR == 62, from
# version_major.h): FF_API_COMPUTE_PKT_FIELDS2, FF_API_INTERNAL_TIMING,
# FF_API_NO_DEFAULT_TLS_VERIFY are all (62 < 63) == true, but none of them
# gate any field inside AVFormatContext/AVStream/AVIOInterruptCB in this
# header revision (no #if FF_API_* blocks appear inside those three struct
# bodies at all). FF_API_R_FRAME_RATE is unconditionally 1 (true); it gates
# the doc comment above AVStream.r_frame_rate only, not the field itself
# (r_frame_rate is unconditional in this header) -- field included.

